%N A316867 Number of times 6 appears in decimal expansion of n.
%H A316867 Chris R. Rehmann, <a href="/A316867/b316867.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..9999</a>
%e A316867 a(0) = 0 since the decimal representation of 0 does not contain the digit 6.
%e A316867 a(6) = 1 since 6 appears once in the decimal expansion of 6.
%p A316867 a:= n-> numboccur(6, convert(n, base, 10)):
%p A316867 seq(a(n), n=1..104);  # _Alois P. Heinz_, Oct 10 2026
%t A316867 Array[ DigitCount[#, 10, 6] &, 105, 0]
%o A316867 (PARI) a(n) = #select(x->x==6, digits(n)); \\ _Michel Marcus_, Jul 20 2018
%o A316867 (MATLAB)
%o A316867 N = 105; a = arrayfun(@(n) length(strfind(num2str(n),'6')),0:min(N-1,flintmax));
%o A316867 disp(regexprep(num2str(a), ' +', ', ')) % _Chris R. Rehmann_, Oct 10 2026
